From ae571549006f2067a51ab9e946345b0a04670d09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:23:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] backends/native: recognize native DisplayID RGB BT.2020
 PQ on eDP

Native DisplayID interface features can describe a complete RGB BT.2020
and ST 2084 tuple without advertising CTA static metadata Type 1. Keep
that tuple separate from the legacy high-level HDR and colorimetry data.
Any parser diagnostic or ordinary/nested CTA HDR or colorimetry block
vetoes this native fallback, including explicit negative CTA metadata.

Map the capability only for eDP with color-mode support, an HDR property
and BT.2020 connector support. Preserve the existing Type 1 path for all
other outputs and retain the actual KMS constructor's shared mapping in
a testable helper. Do not fabricate static metadata or luminance.

Require the parsed low-level DisplayID API with a configure compile/link
probe. Synthetic EDID regressions exercise complete tuples, seventh-slot
additional pairs, split-block negatives, CTA authority in both orders,
malformed encapsulations and every device/connector/property gate.

This is a local review candidate; compiler and runtime qualification are
pending the pre-build review. Normative-spec cross-check and any public
submission remain separate prerequisites.
